.TH TDE-JOURNAL-VIEWER 1 "November 2026" "tde-systemd 1.0.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde-journal-viewer \- view and maintain the systemd journal in TDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde-journal-viewer
[\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\fR]
[\fB\-\-unit\fR \fIunit\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIlevel\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-boot\fR \fIoffset\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-follow\fR]
[\fB\-\-maintenance\fR]
[\fIgeneric TDE and Qt options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde-journal-viewer
shows the messages collected by
.BR systemd-journald (8).
It reads either the system journal or the journal of the user's session
and filters it by boot, priority, unit, syslog identifier, time range,
message text (regular expression) and kernel messages. Messages are
colored by priority; selecting a message shows all of its journal fields.
New messages can be followed as they arrive, and the visible messages can
be exported to a text file.
.PP
Normal users only see their own messages unless they are members of the
\fBsystemd-journal\fR or \fBadm\fR group. The option \fIRead all as
administrator\fR reads the complete journal through
.BR tde-systemd-helper (8)
after polkit authorization.
.PP
The \fIJournal Maintenance\fR dialog shows the disk usage of the journal
and can vacuum old entries by size, age or number of files, rotate,
flush, sync and verify the journal files, and show the active
\fBjournald.conf\fR(5). These operations require authorization.
.PP
The same functionality is available as the TDE Control Center module
\fBSystem Journal\fR (\fBtdecmshell tdejournal\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user
Show the journal of the user session instead of the system journal.
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " unit"
Show only messages of \fIunit\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-priority " \fIlevel\fR"
Show only messages of priority \fIlevel\fR or more important, where 0 is
emergency, 3 error, 4 warning, 6 info and 7 debug.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-boot " \fIoffset\fR"
Show messages of the given boot: \fB0\fR is the current boot, \fB\-1\fR the
previous one, \fBall\fR shows all boots.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Follow new messages.
.TP
.B \-\-maintenance
Open the journal maintenance dialog after start.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F5
Reload the journal with the current filter.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Start or stop following new messages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Export the visible messages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Clear all filters.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Open the maintenance dialog.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tde-journal-viewer \-\-unit ssh.service \-\-follow
Watch the log of the SSH server.
.TP
.B tde-journal-viewer \-p 3 \-b \-1
Show the errors of the previous boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tde-systemd-manager (1),
.BR tde-systemd-helper (8),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd-journald (8),
.BR journald.conf (5)
.PP
The complete handbook is available in the TDE Help Center
(\fBkhelpcenter help:/tde-systemd/journal.html\fR).
